    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Q3 beat and Google deal swamped by AI selloff; CEG near 52-week low",
               "summary":  "Constellation\u0027s own news since October has been strong. It signed a 20-year Google deal on Oct 6 and won a conditional DOE loan guarantee of up to $5.0B for uprates on Oct 27. On Nov 9 it beat Q3 estimates with adjusted EPS of $5.06, against $3.04 a year earlier, and lifted 2026 guidance to $12.50–12.80. The stock jumped 10.5% that day. It then lost 15.3% in the week to Nov 20 as an AI-led market correction hit. At $237.41 it trades below all three EMAs, on its lower Bollinger Band, and only 3.8% above its 52-week low.",
               "pros":  [
                            "Q3 adjusted EPS of $5.06 beat estimates near $3.90, and 2026 guidance rose to $12.50–12.80 from $11.50–12.50.",
                            "Google signed a 20-year PPA tied to about 890 MW of uprates, plus a 15-year 2,700 MW load-following deal (Oct 6).",
                            "Amazon\u0027s 20-year, 690 MW deal backs more than $3B of investment at Calvert Cliffs, including a 190 MW expansion.",
                            "A conditional DOE guarantee of up to $5.0B, at 0.375% over Treasuries, makes uprate funding cheaper.",
                            "Brokers kept raising targets during the drop (BMO to $335), and none of the 25 covering firms rates it sell."
